{"nodes": [{"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_document", "label": "QR, Barcode and Scan Architecture", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_dual_label_identity", "label": "Dual-Label Identity (Code128 + Opaque QR)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Primary key, manufacturer serial, IMEI, customer name, cost and job details must never appear in the QR payload, and a repair job gets its own token so a device QR cannot silently come to mean 'current job'."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_identifier_classes", "label": "Identifier Classes and Mutability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tokens may rotate while identity stays fixed; POS SKU is explicitly not physical-unit identity."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_qr_payload", "label": "HTTPS Resolver QR Payload", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An HTTPS URL opens in ordinary phone cameras, lets routing evolve without reprinting identity, resists enumeration through the opaque token, lets the server choose the destination, and allows rotation after suspected disclosure."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_public_resolver", "label": "Public GET Resolver Behavior", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unknown, revoked, cross-business and unauthorized tokens receive indistinguishable safe responses, and the post-login redirect uses a fresh internal URL that does not retain the raw token."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_scan_resolve_api", "label": "POST /recommerce/scans/resolve API", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolution never performs the selected business action itself; mutation endpoints take their own idempotency key and expected version."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_code128_label_service", "label": "Device/Job Label Service over milon/barcode", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The existing POS label loop repeats catalog variation data per quantity and cannot emit one distinct physical-unit token per label, so Recommerce needs its own label service while reusing the low-level rendering and geometry utilities."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_label_content_policy", "label": "Label Content Policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Customer name/phone, passcode, full IMEI, purchase cost, diagnosis and repair issue are never printed because a label is a publicly visible surface."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_keyboard_wedge_scanning", "label": "Keyboard-Wedge Scanner Path", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The primary Alpha hardware path must submit on Enter immediately rather than relying on the existing POS autocomplete delay, and must keep raw key bursts out of unrelated form fields."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_camera_scanning", "label": "Camera Scanning with BarcodeDetector", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a77.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Camera scanning is convenience, not the sole Alpha path; the fallback decoder is locally bundled and security-reviewed rather than loaded from a public CDN."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_batch_label_generation", "label": "Batch Label Generation and Print Manifest", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A failed print creates no new devices or tokens, and 'printed' is operational evidence rather than proof the label was physically attached."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_contextual_scan_actions", "label": "Contextual Scan Action Resolution", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The server derives allowed actions from permission, location, state, reservation and ownership; client-provided context cannot override eligibility."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_duplicate_and_replay_handling", "label": "Duplicate Read and Replay Handling", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Opening a token is harmless, so replay defense concentrates on mutations via unique (business_id, command_type, idempotency_key) plus stored outcomes."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_scan_security_controls", "label": "Scan URL and Token Security Controls", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a711", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Opaque QR tokens reduce enumeration risk but are explicitly not authentication credentials for business actions."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_offline_behavior", "label": "Online-Only Alpha Scan Behavior", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a712", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A browser cannot confirm ownership, state or stock without the server, and a service-worker cache alone is insufficient; offline would need a signed command journal, conflict policy, device trust model and reconciliation UX."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_mobile_channel_neutrality", "label": "Channel-Neutral Contract for Future Mobile App", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a714", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolver URLs, scan API contract and idempotency contract are channel-neutral so a future app reuses the same services; it must not gain authority merely because it scanned a QR."}, {"id": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_scan_monitoring_and_tests", "label": "Scan Monitoring and Required Tests", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a713", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_dual_label_identity", "target": "recommerce_architecture_canonical_physical_device", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_qr_payload", "target": "recommerce_data_model_recommerce_scan_tokens", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_public_resolver", "target": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_qr_payload", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_scan_resolve_api", "target": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_contextual_scan_actions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.2 / \u00a79", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_scan_resolve_api", "target": "recommerce_architecture_permissions_and_tenancy", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a74.2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_code128_label_service", "target": "recommerce_data_model_recommerce_label_jobs", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recommerce_qr_scan_architecture_batch_label_generation", "target": "recommerce_data_model_recommerce_label_job_items", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "RECOMMERCE_QR_SCAN_ARCHITECTURE.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "weight": 1.0}, {"s